\begin{align*}
\det \begin{pmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{pmatrix} &= 0 \\
\Leftrightarrow (a + b + c)( ab + ac + bc - a^2 - b^2 - c^2) &= 0.
\end{align*}
If the first factor is 0, then either $a + b = 0$ or $b + c = 0$ or $c + a = 0.$  In each case, the given expression is equal to
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = \frac{a - b}{a + b} + \frac{a - c}{a + c} + \frac{b - c}{b + c}.\] We can telescope this to get 0, by writing the fractions with a common denominator:
\[\frac{(a - b)(a + c) + (a - c)(b + c) + (b - c)(a + c)}{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}.\] The numerator can be rearranged as
\[(a^2 - b^2 + a^2 - c^2) + (b^2 - c^2 + ab + bc) + (ac + bc - c^2),\] which is equal to 0 by symmetry.

